          "content": {
            "id": "cont-cdf-to-pdf-root",
            "type": "question",
            "label": "1",
            "prompt": "The continuous random variable $X$ has cumulative distribution function\n$$F(x)=\\begin{cases}0,&x<0,\\\\\\dfrac{x^2+2x}{24},&0\\le x\\le4,\\\\1,&x>4.\\end{cases}$$\nFind the PDF $f(x)$ of $X$, stating its values for all $x$.",
            "answerSpaceMm": 30,
            "answer": {
              "short": "$f(x)=\\begin{cases}\\dfrac{x+1}{12},&0\\le x\\le4,\\\\0,&\\text{otherwise}.\\end{cases}$",
              "worked": "The PDF is the derivative of the CDF. For $0<x<4$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=F'(x)\\\\f(x)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{x^2+2x}{24}\\right)\\\\f(x)&=\\frac{2x+2}{24}\\\\f(x)&=\\frac{x+1}{12}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x<0$ and $x>4$, $F(x)$ is constant, so $f(x)=0$.\nHence $f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{12}$ for $0\\le x\\le4$, and $0$ otherwise."
            }
          }
        },
