            "worked": "The PDF is the derivative of the CDF. For $0<x<4$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=F'(x)\\\\f(x)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{x^2+2x}{24}\\right)\\\\f(x)&=\\frac{2x+2}{24}\\\\f(x)&=\\frac{x+1}{12}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x<0$ and $x>4$, $F(x)$ is constant, so $f(x)=0$.\nHence $f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{12}$ for $0\\le x\\le4$, and $0$ otherwise."
